    "title": "Session identity hardening and clearer chat error surfaces",
    "intro": "Today's nightly focuses on backend correctness and interface clarity: dev-loop automaton runs now demand a stable session ID up front, hosted workspace file requests no longer cross-contaminate between users on Aura Web, and both desktop chat and the mobile input bar do a better job explaining what went wrong and what's required to send.",
    "entries": [
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-1",
        "time_label": "12:35 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-08-31T07:35:01.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-08-31T07:35:01.000Z",
        "title": "Dev-loop automaton runs require a stable session ID",
        "summary": "The automaton start contract now treats aura_session_id as mandatory instead of optional, so router and billing telemetry can reliably distinguish concurrent dev-loop runs.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Promoted aura_session_id from Option<String> to a required String across the harness AutomatonStartParams and dev-loop start params, ensuring bootstrap and continuation requests always carry an X-Aura-Session-Id header rather than being silently rejected downstream.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "c649557c235b97ce6f94ced0a943e042b20fe225"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Updated server-side identity validation and shape logging to check for a non-empty session string, and refreshed harness tests to cover the new non-optional contract.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "c649557c235b97ce6f94ced0a943e042b20fe225"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-2",
        "time_label": "7:26 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-08-31T14:26:24.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-08-31T14:26:24.000Z",
        "title": "Hosted workspace file auth no longer leaks across concurrent web users",
        "summary": "Fixed a cross-user auth race on Aura Web where hosted workspace file requests could be re-issued under another user's cached JWT and return spurious 404s.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Hosted workspace file handlers now resolve the parent agent using the incoming request's JWT via the network client instead of AgentInstanceService, which pulled from a process-wide SettingsStore that concurrent users were overwriting.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "10890eb06aafb912f34794ce5e334cd2e07535c7"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Added a dedicated hosted_workspace_auth_race integration test that exercises overlapping requests from two different user tokens to lock in the fix.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "10890eb06aafb912f34794ce5e334cd2e07535c7"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-3",
        "time_label": "8:21 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-08-31T15:21:32.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-08-31T15:22:11.000Z",
        "title": "Clearer tool error panels and remote-agent guidance in chat",
        "summary": "Chat tool blocks now render structured error responses with retry timing and guidance, and the mobile input bar explains when sending requires a remote agent while making tap-to-send more reliable.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Generic tool blocks parse errored results into a titled panel with message, retry-after countdown, guidance list, and HTTP/code metadata instead of dumping raw JSON, backed by new parseToolError and formatRetryDelay utilities.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "b4fcc9610712db42c6269b96816bdfae7ecb0716"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "MobileChatInputBar gained a disabled-state notice and a remote-required status indicator that clarifies when a remote agent is needed, plus stabilized tap-send behavior covered by a new test suite.",
            "commit_shas": [
